<%- include('../partials/header', { title: 'The Chronicle' }) %>
<%
  const german = A.german;
  const flag = name => [...german].some(g => String(name).includes(g)) ? '🇩🇪' : '🇺🇸';
  const dollars = n => (n == null ? '' : '$' + Number(n).toLocaleString('en-US'));
  const champByYear = {};
  for (const c of A.champions) champByYear[c.year] = c;
  const years = [];
  for (let y = 2026; y >= (A.lore.foundingYear || 2016); y--) years.push(y);
  // Season pages exist where box scores do (2023-2025); the pre-Sleeper years
  // (2016-2022) share one ceremonial chapter at /history/early. 2026 is live,
  // no page yet.
  const linkFor = y => A.byYear[y] ? `/history/season/${y}` : (y >= 2016 && y <= 2022 ? '/history/early' : null);
%>

<div class="chron">
  <!-- 1. HEADER (turnover-corrected eyebrow) -->
  <p class="chron-eyebrow">Est. 2016 · Not Quite the Same Ten Men · A Decade of Receipts</p>
  <h1 class="chron-title">The <span class="gold">MFGA</span> Archive</h1>
  <p class="chron-sub">Every dollar, every champion, every humiliation — written down at last.</p>

  <!-- 2. THE STORY OF THE LEAGUE (the centerpiece) -->
  <div class="card">
    <div class="body">
      <div class="chapter">
        <p>It started with a dick joke. 2016, ten guys, a hundred bucks each, and a
        league called Balls and Wieners — picked by adults with jobs and children.
        That became the Whiny Little Bitch League, which fit better, and in 2024
        somebody decided we should be Make Football Great Again. Three names, none of
        them sayable in front of your mother.</p>

        <p>The buy-in went up every year like a bad mortgage — a hundred, one
        twenty-five, one fifty, on up to four hundred, with a vote on the floor to
        make it five. David has objected to every increase since the year he won it.</p>

        <p>Then in 2023 we added a hundred a week to the top score. Nobody thought
        much about it. It's now thirty-seven percent of the pot — the biggest prize
        in the league, and none of us voted for it to be that.</p>

        <p>Three guys aren't here anymore. Sam, Dylan and Jeremy took the chairs
        Brandon, Taylor Hagen and Tori left behind. The records barely remember them
        — two are scrubbed out entirely, one survives as a name in a single draft
        order. They're in here anyway.</p>

        <h3><span class="n">§</span> The Decade</h3>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/early">2016.</a></strong> Balls and Wieners, year
        one, <span class="stat">$100</span> a man. David won it for
        <span class="stat">$300</span>. No box scores survive, so that's all there is.</p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/early">2017.</a></strong> Cory won it,
        <span class="stat">$375</span>, buy-in up to $125.</p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/early">2018.</a></strong> Cory won it again,
        <span class="stat">$450</span>, back-to-back. He hasn't won since. It's been
        six years.</p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/early">2019.</a></strong> Marian, <span class="stat">$600</span>.
        The start of the run.</p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/early">2020.</a></strong> Marian again, <span class="stat">$750</span>.</p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/early">2021.</a></strong> Marian a third straight
        time, <span class="stat">$900</span>. Nobody else had gotten a look in three
        years.</p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/early">2022.</a></strong> Marian and Sam split the
        title, <span class="stat">$1,050</span> between them — the fourth Marian ring
        in four years and the only one anyone disputes. That's the asterisk; it's
        explained at the bottom.</p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/season/2023">2023.</a></strong> Last year as the
        Whiny Little Bitch League, and the year the weekly hundred quietly appeared.
        Michael won it clean — <span class="stat">95–40</span> against the field and
        the most points in the league — the first of his. Dylan made the final and
        lost it, still the closest he's ever gotten. Justin went
        <span class="stat">71–64</span> against everyone and finished 6–9 with
        <span class="stat">$0</span>; Cory finished 9–6 and cashed on a
        <span class="stat">.422</span> team, the worst-scoring lineup of anyone who
        made money. David dropped the year's high, <span class="stat">171.50</span>,
        and blew Sam out by <span class="stat">98.40</span>.
        <a href="/history/season/2023">Full chapter →</a></p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/season/2024">2024.</a></strong> We became Make
        Football Great Again and added keepers. Jeremy won it off the two-seed. David
        took the regular season and the biggest check, then went out fourth in the
        playoffs. Cory scored the <em>second-most points in the league</em> and
        missed the bracket entirely — <span class="stat">8.20</span> behind Marian on
        the season tiebreaker, with <span class="stat">297</span> left on his bench.
        Michael's Josh Allen went for <span class="stat">57.88</span> and Michael
        still went 6–9. <a href="/history/season/2024">Full chapter →</a></p>

        <p><strong><a href="/history/season/2025">2025.</a></strong> Michael again —
        <span class="stat">12–3</span>, <span class="stat">$1,325</span>, the richest
        year on record — two titles in three years now. Richard scored
        <span class="stat">1,711</span> points, third-most in the league, and finished
        <em>dead last</em> at <span class="stat">4–11</span>, the worst luck anyone's
        ever had here. Bates rode Gibbs to a runner-up and is still without a ring;
        Cory went 5–10 and named the team Scheisse. <a href="/history/season/2025">Full chapter →</a></p>

        <p><strong>2026.</strong> In progress. Buy-in's $400 with a vote to make it
        five. For the record: Marian's up about <span class="stat">$5,000</span>
        all-time, Justin's barely cleared <span class="stat">$600</span>, and Dylan,
        Bates, Richard and Justin have never won the thing. The buy-in ladder, the
        payouts and the pending votes live in <a href="/history/amendments">the
        Amendments</a>; everything else is below.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 3. THE SEASONS timeline -->
  <div class="card">
    <h2>📖 The Seasons <span class="sub">tap a year with a chapter</span></h2>
    <div class="body">
      <div class="timeline">
        <% for (const y of years) {
             const c = champByYear[y];
             const href = linkFor(y);
             const written = chapters.has(y);
             const preSleeper = y < 2023;
             const inProgress = y === 2026;
        %>
          <% if (href) { %><a class="tl-row" href="<%= href %>"><% } else { %><div class="tl-row tl-dead"><% } %>
            <span class="tl-year"><%= y %></span>
            <span class="tl-mid">
              <% if (inProgress) { %>
                <span class="tl-champ tl-live">Season in progress</span>
              <% } else if (c) { %>
                <span class="tl-champ">🏆 <%= c.champion %> <span class="flag"><%= flag(c.champion) %></span><% if (c.asterisk) { %><a class="aster" href="#asterisk" onclick="event.stopPropagation()">*</a><% } %></span>
                <% if (c.payout != null) { %><span class="tl-won"><%= dollars(c.payout) %></span><% } %>
              <% } %>
            </span>
            <span class="tl-tag">
              <% if (written) { %><span class="tag">Chapter</span>
              <% } else if (A.byYear[y]) { %><span class="tag pending">Records</span>
              <% } else if (preSleeper) { %><span class="tag ghost">Pre-Sleeper</span>
              <% } %>
            </span>
          <% if (href) { %></a><% } else { %></div><% } %>
        <% } %>
      </div>
      <p class="tl-note">Full box scores survive from <b>2023</b> on. 2016–2022 are the age before Sleeper — champions and money only; their chapters are on the way.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 4. FOUR DOORS -->
  <div class="doors">
    <a class="door" href="/history/records">
      <span class="door-icon">📖</span>
      <span class="door-title">The Record Book</span>
      <span class="door-sub">All-time highs, lows, the dynasty tracker, and every franchise page.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="door" href="/history/money">
      <span class="door-icon">💰</span>
      <span class="door-title">The Money Board</span>
      <span class="door-sub">Career earnings, ranked ten deep. The table that settles arguments.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="door" href="/history/badbeats">
      <span class="door-icon">💔</span>
      <span class="door-title">Bad Beats Hall of Fame</span>
      <span class="door-sub">Auto-detected heartbreak — the tragedies the schedule authored.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="door" href="/history/catalogue">
      <span class="door-icon">🃏</span>
      <span class="door-title">The Absurdity Catalogue</span>
      <span class="door-sub">Every box score mined: kickers over QBs, benched studs, near-misses.</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <!-- 5. THE 2022 ASTERISK (closing footnote) -->
  <%- include('_asterisk') %>

  <p class="provenance">
    Derived from the master sheet (<%= A.provenance.master_sha256.slice(0, 12) %>…)
    and the Sleeper harvest of <%= (A.provenance.harvest_built_at || '').slice(0, 10) %>.
  </p>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
